{
  "about": [
    "Which museum objects and runway tags count as evidence of each trend. Edit by hand, then rerun scripts/assemble.mjs.",
    "Keys are trend ids from parts/trends.json. Trends with no entry get no counts or examples.",
    "met: Met object names, lowercased, as in parts/met.json countsByTypeYear.",
    "runway: Vogue Runway tags, lowercased, as in parts/runway.json shareByTagYear. A trend with several tags takes the largest share in each year, since looks can carry more than one tag.",
    "vam: a list of rules over V&A objects in parts/vam.json. A plain string matches the object type exactly. An object rule matches when every field it has matches: type (list of exact types), material (list, any of the object's materials), colour (list, any of the object's colours), title and designer (case-insensitive regular expressions), from and to (object year, inclusive).",
    "Be conservative: only map a type when it clearly is the trend. A Met evening dress is not a trend by itself."
  ],
